1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Pick any spot on the sky. SkyDrift gathers every SPHEREx picture of it.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
SPHEREx sees each spot at a different wavelength every time, so a raw blink flickers.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Stacking per visit and per detector keeps only real changes.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
The coldest known brown dwarf: invisible at 1 µm, bright at 4.6 µm.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
SkyDrift finds movers itself and measures how far they went.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
And it checks itself against known stars. Try it on any patch of sky.
